        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Flavin, Peter Benchley, George Archainbaud, Beulah Marie Dix, Steven Spielberg\n- Works: Three Who Loved, Jaws, Jaws novel\n- Topics: American writers, film adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Martin Flavin, born in 1883 and died in 1967, was an American playwright and novelist.\n- Three Who Loved is a 1931 American Pre-Code drama film directed by George Archainbaud.\n- Three Who Loved was written from a screenplay by Beulah Marie Dix based on a story by Pulitzer Prize-winning author Martin Flavin.\n- Peter Benchley, born in 1940 and died in 2006, was an American author and screenwriter.\n- Peter Benchley wrote the 1974 novel Jaws.\n- Jaws is a 1975 American thriller film directed by Steven Spielberg and based on Peter Benchley’s 1974 novel of the same name.",
